  "summary": "Cyrus SASL through 2.1.28 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in the SRP server mechanism because…",
  "details": "Cyrus SASL through 2.1.28 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in the SRP server mechanism because srp_server_mech_step2 does not reject client public values A that are multiples of N. Unauthenticated network clients can send A equal to N to force a zero shared secret, authenticating as any existing user without the password and learning session keys.",
